  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora: Voluntary Core Contribution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES; at times also referred to as the Washington Convention) is a multilateral agreement that aims to ensure that international trade in animals and plants does not threaten their survival in the wild. It accords varying degrees of protection to more than 40,000 species. Funding by the Australian Department of Climate Change, Energy, the Environment and Water represents Australia&apos;s annual voluntary contribution to the agreement.</narrative>
  </description>
